    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nInterested in this property? Sign up for mySherryFitz to arrange your viewing, see current offers or make your own offer. Register now at SherryFitz.ie\nSherry FitzGerald O'Reilly welcome you to 29 Hunterswood, a fine 3 bedroomed mid terrace home in a prime location in Sallins village. This home offers an excellent layout, spacious rear garden and the space for an attic conversion ( subject to planning permission).\nIt is conveniently located with, the primary school, GAA club, playground, an array of restaurants, bars, shops, and the extended Grand Canal Greenway all just a short stroll away. A short drive will take you to Monread Shopping Centre or Naas town, offering a fine selection of shops, retail parks, schools, restaurants, cinema, theatre, and many sports facilities. Hunterswood is ideally located for the commuter, it is a short walk to the Sallins Train Station for direct routes to Heuston and Connolly Stations, or a five-minute drive to the N7/M7 junctions, while the bus stops nearby provide services to a wide range of towns.\nAccommodation comprises entrance hallway, kitchen/dining room, living room, guest wc and utility. Upstairs 3 bedrooms (one en-suite), bathroom, boiler room."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nHallway - 6.29m x 1.93m\nThe welcoming hallway has a porcelain tiled floor and new carpet laid on the stairs. With storage closet off (2.47m x 0.75m).\n\nLiving Room - 4.74m x 4.7m\nThe spacious living room features French doors leading to the rear garden. It is floored in a warm walnut laminate and includes an attractive cast iron fireplace with wooden surround and granite hearth.\n\nKitchen/Dining Room - 5.37m x 2.81m\nThe bright kitchen/dining room, with front aspect, features a range of shaker style cabinets with a tiled splashback and tiled floor. It includes an oven, 5 ring gas hob, fridge freezer and integrated dishwasher.\n\nUtility Room - 1.56m x 1.36m\nLocated off the hallway, with tile floor, worktop, washing machine, dryer and door to guest wc.\n\nGuest WC - 1.56m x 1.28m\nThe guest wc includes wc and washbasin, with tile floor.\n\nUpstairs - \n\n\nLanding - 4.27m x 1.95m\nThe landing has a new carpet floor and includes both a hotpress off and a storage room which houses the gas boiler (0.93 x 0.8m). There is attic access via a ladder stair. The attic is part floored and has two Velux windows. It may be suitable for conversion to further accommodation.\n\nBedroom 1 - 4.75m x 3.47m\nThis spacious double bedroom to front has a selection of fitted wardrobes and a new carpet floor.\n\nEn-Suite - 2.75m x 1.07m\nWith wc, wash basin and shower cabinet. The floor and shower are tiled, featuring mosaic detailing.\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.32m x 2.54m\nThis double bedroom overlooks the rear garden. It has a tv point, carpet floor and fitted wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.14m x 2.05m\nWith rear view, this is a single bedroom floored in carpet and including a wardrobe.\n\nBathroom - 2.75m x 1.81m\nThe family bathroom comprises a wc, wash hand basin, and bath with overhead shower. The floor and bath surrounds are tiled.\n\nOutside - \nTo front there is allocated parking for one car. The rear garden is in lawn.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Built circa 2006.</li><li>Extends to 103m2 approximately.</li><li>Double glazed windows.</li><li>Natural gas central heating.</li><li>Low maintenance exterior.</li><li>Fitted with intruder alarm system.</li><li>uPVC soffit and fascia.</li><li>New carpets.</li><li>Freshly painted.</li><li>ladder stairs to part floored attic with Velux windows. </li><li>All listed appliances included.</li><li>Allocated parking plus visitor parking.</li><li>Spacious rear garden.</li><li>A short stroll to Sallins Village with its selection of shops, restaurants, school and Grand Canal greenway.</li><li>Just a few minutes from Naas with its many shops, restaurants, Secondary schools, hospital, theatre, library, cinema and many sporting facilities.</li><li>A 5-minute walk to the Sallins train Station with access to Heuston and Connolly Stations.</li><li>Bus stop nearby for 139 buses with route including Maynooth University, Intel Leixlip and IT Blanchardstown.</li><li>Short drive to Junctions 9 or 9a of the N7/M7.</ul>"
      },
